                            	  7366:     ; If the player is at an "open", "key", or "shutter" door,
                            	  7367:     ; then the player walked all the way to the edge of the play
                            	  7368:     ; area. So, use index 2 to set Link's relative position to 0.
                            	  7369:     ;
                            	  7370:     ; Otherwise, the player is at wall level. Link has to walk to the
                            	  7371:     ; edge of the play area. So, set a relative position that
                            	  7372:     ; reflects that distance: $28 or -$28.
                            	  7373:     ;
                            	  7374:     ; If walking in a decreasing direction (left or up), then
                            	  7375:     ; Link's relative position is $28 and has to decrease to 0.
                            	  7376:     ;
                            	  7377:     ; If walking in an increasing direction (right or down), then
                            	  7378:     ; Link's relative position is -$28 and has to increase to 0.
                            	  7379:     ;
